# Test: x_1^3 in n=3 (Veronese P^2 in P^9; ideal generated by 2x2 minors of 3x3 catalecticant?)
# Actually for n=3 d=3, Sym^3 V_3 has dim 10. Veronese of P^2 in P^9 has dim 2.
# I_2 = ideal of Veronese surface = 2x2 minors of catalecticant matrix.
n, d = 3, 3
syms_full = sp.symbols(f'x1:{n+1}')
